/*
  The storyboard's sentence, for all 185 steps.

  The storyboard row draws pictures and nothing else now — that was the point
  of removing its caption. What the column MEANS lives in `steps.summary`, and
  176 of 185 steps had none, so the row that was supposed to make a column
  legible said "Not specified" in every panel.

  Each summary is written FROM that step's own cells: the actor lanes say what
  each role does, the tech lanes name the touchpoint, and the summary is the
  one sentence across them. Nothing here is new fact — where a step's cells
  only describe planned work, the summary says "Planned:" and stops.

  Warm-Up's nine were written earlier as the calibration run and set the
  voice: present tense, name the actors, name the system only where it
  matters.
*/
begin;

update public.steps as s set summary = v.summary
from (values
  ('a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000711', 'A prospective tutor hears about PLUS from a current or former tutor.'),
